ll, "list_has_generated": null, "main_agent_searched": false, "model": "claude-opus-5-5", "model_context_window": 1000000, "model_max_tokens": 128000, "output_tail": "Adding a regression test, then running.\n`round_money(2.675)` now returns `2.68`.\n\n**Why it happened:** a float can't hold 2.675 exactly. It's stored as `2.67499999999999982\u2026`, so Python's `round()` correctly rounds that down to 2.67. Separately, `round()` rounds exact halves to the nearest even digit (so `0.125` became `0.12`), which also broke the \"half up\" promise in the docstring.\n\n**The fix** (`pricing/money.py`): `round_money` now takes the number as it's normally printed (`repr(x)`, which gives `\"2.675\"`), rounds that as a `Decimal` with `ROUND_HALF_UP`, and returns a float as before. Negative halves round away from zero (`-2.675` \u2192 `-2.68`).\n\n**Checks:** pytest isn't installed here, so I didn't run the test suite. I called the functions directly instead:\n- `2.675\u21922.68`, `1.005\u21921.01`, `0.125\u21920.13`, `2.674\u21922.67`, `-2.675\u2192-2.68`, `3\u21923.0`\n- `add_vat(10)` \u2192 `12.0`\n- `split(10.00, 3)` \u2192 `[3.34, 3.33, 3.33]`, unchanged\n\nI added `tests/test_round_money.py` covering those cases. It needs `pytest` installed to run.\n\n**Remaining risk:** `add_vat` multiplies floats before rounding. If that multiplication itself lands just under a half (e.g. it prints as `x.xx4999999\u2026`), it will still round down. If that matters, prices and the VAT rate need to be `Decimal` from the start, which is a bigger change than this fix.", "paced_wait_s": 0.0, "permission_rejections": 0, "read_calls": 2, "replies_ok": 9, "replies_throttled": 0, "requests_cache_read": 242103, "requests_cache_write": 15989, "requests_cost_usd": 0.1714056, "requests_count": 9, "requests_input_uncached": 20, "requests_output": 2148, "reread": false, "rule_order": "none", "rule_prefix": "neither", "run_id": "omp:trig-omp-bugfix-regress:claude-opus-5-5:trial12", "run_seed": 20261014, 